    content:
      "These Beef Tacos are a weeknight favourite: well-spiced minced beef simmered until saucy, piled into crisp shells with cool, crunchy toppings.\n\n### Ingredients:\n\n**For the beef:**\n\n* 1 tbsp (15 ml) neutral oil\n* 1 small onion (about 100 g), finely chopped\n* 2 garlic cloves, finely chopped\n* 500 g minced beef (15–20% fat)\n* 2 tsp (10 ml) chilli powder (mild blend)\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) ground cumin\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) smoked paprika\n* 1/2 tsp (2.5 ml) dried oregano (Mexican if possible)\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) salt\n* 1 tbsp (15 g) tomato paste\n* 120 ml water\n\n**To serve:**\n\n* 8 hard taco shells\n* 100 g iceberg lettuce, finely shredded\n* 2 medium tomatoes (about 250 g), diced\n* 80 g cheddar or Monterey Jack, grated\n* 100 g soured cream\n* Small handful fresh coriander, chopped\n* 1 lime, cut into wedges\n* Salsa or hot sauce, to taste\n\n### Instructions:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 180°C.\n2. Heat the oil in a 28 cm frying pan over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook for 3 minutes until softened.\n3. Add the beef and cook for 5–6 minutes, breaking it up with a spoon, until no pink remains and the edges begin to brown. Spoon off excess fat if there is more than 1–2 tbsp.\n4. Stir in the garlic, spices, oregano and salt and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.\n5. Add the tomato paste and water, then simmer for 4–5 minutes, stirring, until the liquid reduces to a thick sauce that coats the meat.\n6. While the beef simmers, stand the taco shells upright in a baking dish and warm them in the oven for 4–5 minutes until crisp and fragrant.\n7. Squeeze a little lime over the beef and taste for seasoning.\n8. Fill each shell with about 2 heaped tablespoons of beef, then top with lettuce, tomato, cheese, soured cream, coriander and salsa. Serve straight away with lime wedges.\n\n### Tips:\n\n* Fill the shells just before eating so they stay crisp.\n* The seasoned beef keeps for 3 days in the fridge and freezes well for up to 3 months.\n* For soft tacos, swap the shells for 15 cm flour or corn tortillas warmed in a dry pan for 20–30 seconds per side.",
