    title: "Gołąbki",
    description:
      "Polish cabbage rolls stuffed with pork, beef and rice, baked in a rich tomato sauce until meltingly tender.",
    difficulty: "medium",
    image: "",
    content:
      'Gołąbki ("little pigeons") are a Polish Sunday and holiday classic: soft white cabbage leaves wrapped around a seasoned meat and rice filling, then gently braised in tomato sauce. They taste even better reheated the next day.\n\n### Ingredients:\n\n**For the rolls:**\n\n* 1 large head white cabbage (about 2 kg)\n* 150 g white rice (uncooked)\n* 500 g minced pork shoulder\n* 250 g minced beef\n* 1 large onion (about 150 g), finely chopped\n* 1 tbsp (15 g) butter\n* 1 egg\n* 1 tsp (2 g) dried marjoram\n* 1½ tsp (9 g) salt\n* ½ tsp (1 g) freshly ground black pepper\n\n**For the sauce:**\n\n* 500 ml passata\n* 2 tbsp (30 g) tomato paste\n* 400 ml beef or vegetable stock\n* 2 bay leaves, 3 allspice berries\n* 1 tsp (4 g) sugar\n* 2 tbsp (30 ml) sour cream 18% (optional, to finish)\n\n### Instructions:\n\n1. Cut the core out of the cabbage with a small knife. Lower the head into a large pot of boiling salted water and simmer for 3–4 minutes, peeling off the outer leaves with tongs as they soften and turn bright green. Repeat until you have about 18 good leaves; cool them on a tray.\n2. Shave down the thick central rib of each leaf with a knife so it rolls easily. Use the small torn leaves to line the bottom of a 24–26 cm heavy casserole or a 30 x 20 cm baking dish.\n3. Cook the rice in boiling salted water for 8 minutes (it should still be firm), drain and cool. Fry the onion in the butter over medium heat for 6–8 minutes until soft and golden.\n4. In a large bowl mix the pork, beef, rice, onion, egg, marjoram, salt and pepper with your hands for 1–2 minutes until evenly combined.\n5. Place about 3 heaped tablespoons (70 g) of filling at the rib end of a leaf, fold in the sides and roll up firmly. Lay the rolls seam-side down in the dish, packed snugly in 1–2 layers.\n6. Whisk together the passata, tomato paste, stock, sugar and a pinch of salt. Pour over the rolls, tuck in the bay leaves and allspice; the liquid should almost cover them. Cover with a lid or foil.\n7. Bake at 180 °C for 1 hour 30 minutes (or simmer covered on the lowest hob heat) until a skewer slides easily through the cabbage and the filling reaches 75 °C.\n8. Tilt the dish, ladle out a little sauce and whisk in the sour cream, then stir it back in. Rest for 10 minutes before serving.\n\n### Tips:\n\n* Serve the Polish way with boiled potatoes or mashed potatoes, spooning plenty of sauce over the top.\n* If the leaves are hard to peel, freeze the whole cabbage overnight and thaw it; the leaves become pliable without boiling.\n* Gołąbki keep 3–4 days refrigerated and freeze well for up to 3 months in their sauce.\n* Do not fully cook the rice beforehand or the filling will turn mushy as it absorbs the sauce.',
